NOTICE of ros2/ralmon_sim/worlds (WS07-T02)

This file states what in this directory is generated, what is third-party, and the licence
situation as found at the sources on 2026-10-09. It is a statement of facts for the human who
decides the release (WS13); it is not legal advice and it does not grant or clear any right.

1. What is generated (authored for this project, no third-party content)

   ward.world, ward_map.pgm and ward_map.yaml are GENERATED by
   ros2/ralmon_sim/scripts/generate_ward_world.py (command: --rooms 6) from a layout of boxes
   written for this project: a corridor, rooms, beds and small tables, as collision and visual
   boxes. The script is deterministic (integer arithmetic, no randomness, no clock); the test
   suite regenerates the files and compares them byte for byte. The files include no third-party
   model, mesh, texture or map and refer to none by URI (no <include> and no model:// reference
   in the SDF; checked by test_world_is_authored_by_the_generator_and_has_no_third_party_reference).
   The dimensions are layout choices of a technical test environment; the world is not a model of a
   real ward. The generated files carry no licence of their own: the licence of the project is
   decided by WS13-T01 (package.xml says NOASSERTION until then).

2. Deviation from the record of WS07-T01 (hospital_world)

   config/package_availability.yaml records the decision "use_ros2_branch" for the hospital world:
   the ros2 branch of aws-robotics/aws-robomaker-hospital-world (commit
   7161eb8448f5cba6a469da7a79ae5d660b0b7f58, built in the image from ros2/sim.repos). WS07-T02 does
   NOT use that world. The ward of the simulation is the generated world of section 1.
   Reasons: the tests and the robot tasks need a map whose free cells, door poses, bedside poses
   and walls are known exactly, a map that is reproducible from the collision geometry of the
   world, and named rooms with poses chosen by this task; deriving that from the 183-include model
   world of the AWS repository would need a mapping pass or a rasterisation of its meshes, which was
   not attempted; and a world without third-party content avoids its open licence question
   (section 3).
   Consequence: the T01 record still says use_ros2_branch (WS07-T01 did not know the needs of the
   tests); the world actually used is the "procedural" option of Passo 3 of the task text (a
   deterministic generator that builds a corridor with N rooms). The AWS world stays built in the image and is not used
   by any launch file or test of this package. Nothing of it is copied into this repository.

