4. Third-party content that is used but not distributed here

   - The PAL Robotics packages tiago_pro_simulation (tiago_pro_gazebo 1.19.0, tiago_pro_bringup
     2.5.1) and pal_gazebo_worlds 4.16.0 are installed from the ROS apt repository by the image;
     their package.xml files declare "Apache License 2.0" (read from the installed files). Nothing of
     them is copied into this repository except what sections 4a and 4b say.
   4a. The physics block of ward.world (ODE solver settings, 1000 Hz update rate, 0.001 s step)
       uses the parameter values found in empty.world, and the friction of the ground plane those of
       corridor_110cm.world, both in pal_gazebo_worlds (read from the installed files); it is a set
       of numbers, not a copy of a file.
   4b. config/nav2_params.yaml is derived from config/nav_public_sim.yaml of the package
       omni_base_2dnav 2.24.2 of PAL Robotics (package.xml: "Apache License 2.0"). The header of
       that file lists the changes. The launch file launch/sim_ward.launch.py adapts the structure
       of tiago_pro_gazebo.launch.py of tiago_pro_gazebo 1.19.0 (package.xml: "Apache License
       2.0"): it keeps the copyright and Apache-2.0 notice of that file as its own header (the text
       was copied from the installed file) and states its changes under it, as section 4 of the
       licence asks for modified files. The full Apache-2.0 licence text is not in the image: the
       Debian copyright files of tiago_pro_gazebo and omni_base_2dnav (read on 2026-10-09) say "See
       repository for full license text". If these derived files are released, WS13 has to take the
       licence text from the PAL repositories or from apache.org and ship it with them; this is an
       open item.
   - Gazebo Classic, Nav2 and ROS 2 packages are used through the image and are not distributed here.

5. Reproduction

   python3 ros2/ralmon_sim/scripts/generate_ward_world.py --rooms 6          (writes the three files)
   python3 ros2/ralmon_sim/scripts/generate_ward_world.py --rooms 6 --check  (exit 1 if they differ)
